<template>
  <section id="market-population" class="market-population">
    <div class="population-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">Participant simulation</p><h2>A virtual market around the chart.</h2></div><span v-if="result.status==='complete'" class="model-badge">{{ result.participant_count }} virtual traders</span></div>
    <div v-if="result.status!=='complete'" class="source-note"><p>{{ result.reason }}</p><p v-if="result.trader_dialogue?.status==='complete'">The {{ result.trader_dialogue.participant_count }} traders completed their discussion. Numerical market paths were not generated.</p></div>
    <template v-else>
      <p class="intro-note">These participants place virtual orders, hold positions and respond to simulated price changes using different behavior rules.<span v-if="result.trader_dialogue"> Each also has a saved opening view, question, reply and memory. Its revised view and risk choices feed the trading policy.</span></p><p v-if="result.trader_dialogue" class="small-note">{{ result.trader_dialogue.changed_decisions }} traders revised their decision controls; {{ result.trader_dialogue.changed_stances }} changed directional stance. The discussion used {{ result.trader_dialogue.model_calls }} batched model calls. These are simulated identities sharing one model.</p>
      <div class="source-note"><strong>{{ result.input_basis.depth_measured ? 'Observed starting depth' : 'Liquidity is assumed' }}</strong><p>{{ result.input_basis.book }}</p><p>{{ result.input_basis.reference }}</p></div>
      <div class="simulation-facts"><div><span>Scenario reference</span><strong>{{ number(result.reference_price) }}</strong></div><div><span>Simulated paths</span><strong>{{ result.scenario_count }}</strong></div><div><span>Clearing rounds</span><strong>{{ result.clearing_rounds }}</strong></div><div><span>Behavior groups</span><strong>{{ result.cohorts.length }}</strong></div></div>
      <p class="small-note">Clearing rounds are model events, not minutes or a forecast deadline. Participant counts and simulated outcomes are not a win probability.</p>
      <div class="case-tabs" role="group" aria-label="Virtual liquidity scenarios"><button v-for="item in result.scenarios" :key="item.id" :class="{selected:caseId===item.id}" @click="caseId=item.id">{{ item.name }} <span>{{ item.depth_multiplier }}× depth</span></button></div>
      <div v-if="scenario" class="population-grid">
        <div>
          <h3>Simulated price paths</h3>
          <svg class="population-chart" viewBox="0 0 760 310" role="img" :aria-label="scenario.name+' simulated price paths'">
            <path :d="band('p10','p90')" class="fan-band"/>
            <path v-for="(path,index) in scenario.sample_paths" :key="index" :d="pathLine(path)" class="example-path"/>
            <path :d="pathLine(scenario.fan.map(point=>point.median))" class="median-line"/>
            <line x1="62" x2="744" :y1="y(result.reference_price)" :y2="y(result.reference_price)" class="reference"/>
            <text x="5" y="24">{{ number(priceRange.high) }}</text><text x="5" y="274">{{ number(priceRange.low) }}</text>
            <text x="64" y="302">Start</text><text x="580" y="302">{{ result.clearing_rounds }} model rounds</text>
          </svg>
          <p class="small-note">Grey paths are individual simulations; orange is the median. The shaded region covers the middle 80% of model paths, not a calibrated market forecast.</p>
          <div class="path-counts"><div v-for="(value,key) in scenario.outcome_counts" :key="key"><strong>{{ value }} / {{ scenario.paths }}</strong><span>{{ outcomeLabel(key) }}</span></div></div>
          <p class="small-note">“Near reference” means within ±{{ number(result.near_reference_band_pct) }}% in this model.</p>
          <div v-if="scenario.before_discussion" class="simulation-takeaway"><h3>What changed after trader discussion?</h3><p>With the same starting inputs and random seed, the median model move changed from {{ number(scenario.before_discussion.median_return_pct) }}% to {{ number(scenario.median_return_pct) }}%. {{ scenario.before_discussion.different_price_paths }} / {{ scenario.paths }} price paths and {{ scenario.before_discussion.changed_actor_activity }} account activity records changed.</p><p class="small-note">This compares opening decisions with revised decisions. It demonstrates influence inside the model, not better forecasting accuracy.</p></div><div class="diagnostics"><span>{{ scenario.diagnostics.partial_fill_steps }} path-rounds with partial fills</span><span>{{ scenario.diagnostics.virtual_stop_events }} virtual stops</span><span>{{ scenario.diagnostics.virtual_liquidation_events }} virtual margin events</span></div>
          <a v-if="scenario.archive" class="download-link" :href="archiveUrl">Download this case’s complete paths and ledgers</a>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>Who is trading?</h3>
          <div class="cohort-list"><article v-for="group in result.cohorts" :key="group.id"><div><strong>{{ group.name }}</strong><span>{{ group.count }} traders · {{ (group.capital_share*100).toFixed(0) }}% of model trader capital</span></div><p>{{ group.behavior }}</p><p class="flow">Model buy volume {{ compact(scenario.cohort_activity[group.family]?.bought) }} · sell volume {{ compact(scenario.cohort_activity[group.family]?.sold) }}</p></article></div>
          <p class="small-note">A separate external liquidity-provider account supplies the remaining depth. Volume is in model units, not verified venue contract volume.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div v-if="takeaway" class="simulation-takeaway"><h3>What the analysts concluded</h3><p>{{ takeaway }}</p></div>
      <details class="population-details"><summary>Example fills and position changes</summary><p class="small-note">A sample of actual computed fills from the first path of the selected case. These are simulation events, not trader chat messages or real executions.</p><div class="data-scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Round</th><th>Participant</th><th>Action</th><th>Bought</th><th>Sold</th><th>Position after</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr v-for="(event,index) in scenario?.events || []" :key="index"><td>{{ event.step+1 }}</td><td>{{ event.agent }}</td><td>{{ actionLabel(event.action) }}</td><td>{{ compact(event.bought) }}</td><td>{{ compact(event.sold) }}</td><td>{{ compact(event.position) }}</td></tr></tbody></table></div></details>
      <details class="population-details"><summary>Inspect the {{ result.participant_count }} virtual participants</summary><p class="small-note">Different starting capital, position, risk limits and information delays make their behavior differ. These profiles are configured assumptions.</p><div class="data-scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Participant</th><th>Capital share</th><th>Information delay</th><th>Virtual leverage</th><th>Holding limit</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr v-for="agent in result.participants" :key="agent.id"><td>{{ agent.name }}</td><td>{{ (agent.capital_weight*100).toFixed(3) }}%</td><td>{{ agent.information_delay }} rounds</td><td>{{ agent.leverage.toFixed(1) }}×</td><td>{{ agent.holding_rounds }} rounds</td></tr></tbody></table></div></details>
      <details class="population-details"><summary>Assumptions and model limits</summary><ul><li v-for="item in result.assumptions" :key="item">{{ item }}</li><li>{{ result.input_basis.move_scale }}</li><li>Assumed taker fee {{ result.cost_assumptions.taker_fee*100 }}%, maker fee {{ result.cost_assumptions.maker_fee*100 }}%, and {{ result.cost_assumptions.slippage_bps }} bps slippage.</li></ul><p class="small-note">Ledger checks: cash plus fees error {{ scenario?.ledger.cash_conservation_error.toExponential(2) }}, net inventory error {{ scenario?.ledger.net_inventory_error.toExponential(2) }}. Passing these checks verifies accounting, not predictive accuracy.</p></details>
    </template>
  </section>
</template>

<script setup>
import {computed} from 'vue'
const props=defineProps({result:{type:Object,required:true},runId:String,takeaway:String,caseId:{type:String,default:'1'}})
const emit=defineEmits(['update:caseId'])
const caseId=computed({get:()=>props.caseId,set:value=>emit('update:caseId',value)})
const scenario=computed(()=>props.result.scenarios?.find(item=>item.id===caseId.value)||props.result.scenarios?.[0])
const priceRange=computed(()=>{const points=scenario.value?.fan||[],examples=scenario.value?.sample_paths?.flat()||[];return {low:Math.min(props.result.reference_price,...points.map(x=>x.p10),...examples),high:Math.max(props.result.reference_price,...points.map(x=>x.p90),...examples)}})
const y=value=>272-(value-priceRange.value.low)/Math.max(priceRange.value.high-priceRange.value.low,1e-8)*250
const x=index=>62+682*index/Math.max(props.result.clearing_rounds,1)
const pathLine=values=>values.map((value,index)=>(index?'L':'M')+x(index)+','+y(value)).join(' ')
const band=(low,high)=>{const points=scenario.value.fan;return pathLine(points.map(point=>point[high]))+points.slice().reverse().map((point,index)=>'L'+x(points.length-1-index)+','+y(point[low])).join(' ')+'Z'}
const number=value=>Number(value).toLocaleString('en-US',{maximumFractionDigits:4})
const compact=value=>Number(value||0).toLocaleString('en-US',{maximumFractionDigits:3})
const outcomeLabel=key=>({above_reference:'Finished above reference',below_reference:'Finished below reference',near_reference:'Finished near reference'}[key]||key)
const actionLabel=value=>({BUY_MARKET:'Market buy',SELL_MARKET:'Market sell',QUOTE_FILL:'Passive quote filled',STOP:'Stop reduction',LIQUIDATE:'Margin liquidation',TAKE_PARTIAL_PROFIT:'Partial profit-taking'}[value]||value)
const api=(import.meta.env.VITE_API_BASE_URL||'http://127.0.0.1:5001').replace(/\/$/,'')
const archiveUrl=computed(()=>api+'/api/chart/analyses/'+props.runId+'/participant-paths/'+scenario.value.id)
</script>

<style scoped>
.market-population{border-top:1px solid #ccc;padding:32px 0;font:13px/1.65 'Helvetica Neue',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;color:#26262c;scroll-margin-top:20px}.population-heading{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;gap:20px}.eyebrow{font-size:10px;letter-spacing:.1em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#888;margin:0 0 7px}.population-heading h2{font-size:27px;line-height:1.2;font-weight:500;letter-spacing:-.025em;margin:0}.model-badge{border:1px solid #ccc;padding:7px 11px;font-size:12px;white-space:nowrap}.intro-note{color:#777;max-width:850px;margin:15px 0}.source-note{background:#fff8f0;border-left:3px solid #bc8752;padding:13px 16px;color:#795634;font-size:12px;margin:20px 0}.source-note strong{font-weight:600}.source-note p{margin:5px 0}.simulation-facts{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr);border:1px solid #ddd;margin:22px 0 10px}.simulation-facts>div{padding:17px;border-right:1px solid #ddd}.simulation-facts>div:last-child{border:0}.simulation-facts span{font-size:11px;color:#888;display:block}.simulation-facts strong{display:block;font-size:27px;font-weight:500;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;margin-top:4px}.small-note{font-size:11px;color:#888;line-height:1.7;margin:12px 0}.case-tabs{display:flex;gap:0;border-bottom:1px solid #ccc;margin:24px 0;overflow-x:auto}.case-tabs button{font-family:inherit;border:0;border-bottom:2px solid transparent;background:white;min-height:49px;padding:10px 15px;white-space:nowrap;color:#777;cursor:pointer}.case-tabs button span{display:block;font-size:10px;color:#999}.case-tabs button.selected{color:#222;border-bottom-color:#ff4f00}.case-tabs button:focus-visible,.population-details summary:focus-visible{outline:3px solid #ff4f00;outline-offset:3px}.population-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1.4fr) minmax(280px,1fr);gap:30px}.market-population h3{font-size:16px;font-weight:500;margin:5px 0 14px}.population-chart{display:block;width:100%;border:1px solid #ddd;background:#f8f8f9;overflow:hidden}.fan-band{fill:#e0e2e5}.example-path{fill:none;stroke:#888;stroke-width:1;opacity:.45}.median-line{fill:none;stroke:#ff4f00;stroke-width:2}.reference{stroke:#aaa;stroke-dasharray:5 5;stroke-width:1}.population-chart text{fill:#777;font-size:11px}.path-counts{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);border-top:1px solid #ddd;margin-top:18px}.path-counts>div{padding:13px 8px 13px 0}.path-counts strong{font-size:19px;font-weight:500;display:block}.path-counts span{font-size:10px;color:#888}.diagnostics{display:flex;gap:8px 18px;flex-wrap:wrap;color:#888;font-size:11px}.download-link{font-size:12px;display:inline-block;color:#ad3d15;margin-top:18px;text-underline-offset:3px}.cohort-list article{border-bottom:1px solid #e2e2e6;padding:10px 0}.cohort-list strong{font-size:13px;font-weight:500}.cohort-list span{display:block;font-size:10px;color:#888}.cohort-list p{font-size:11px;color:#777;margin:6px 0}.cohort-list .flow{font-size:10px;color:#999}.simulation-takeaway{border-left:3px solid #ff4f00;background:#f7f7f8;padding:17px 20px;margin:25px 0}.simulation-takeaway p{font-size:13px;color:#666;margin:0}.population-details{border-top:1px solid #ddd;padding:16px 0;font-size:12px;color:#777}.population-details summary{cursor:pointer;color:#333}.population-details ul{padding-left:18px}.population-details li{margin:8px 0}.data-scroll{overflow:auto;max-height:360px;margin-top:15px}.data-scroll table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;font-size:11px}.data-scroll th,.data-scroll td{padding:9px 12px 9px 0;border-bottom:1px solid #e5e5e8;text-align:left;white-space:nowrap;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}.data-scroll th{font-weight:500;color:#888;position:sticky;top:0;background:white}.market-population p{overflow-wrap:anywhere}@media(max-width:900px){.population-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}}@media(max-width:550px){.population-heading{align-items:flex-start;flex-direction:column;gap:12px}.population-heading h2{font-size:23px}.simulation-facts{grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr}.simulation-facts>div{padding:12px;border-bottom:1px solid #ddd}.simulation-facts>div:nth-child(2){border-right:0}.simulation-facts strong{font-size:23px}.path-counts strong{font-size:17px}.case-tabs button{font-size:11px;padding:10px}.simulation-takeaway{padding:14px}.population-chart text{font-size:13px}}
</style>
